act\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-017\"},\"result_id\":\"RESULT-017\",\"schema\":\"bounded-host-applied-candidate-effect-receipt-v0\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"upsert_decision_section\",\"body\":\"Route-blue service at TRN-065 v8 reports 88.3 percent availability as current [TRANSIT]. Paratransit service at TRN-066 v8 reports 90.0 percent availability as current [TRANSIT]. These are distinct accessibility gates: route-blue covers standard accessible routes, while paratransit serves mobility-restricted populations; neither may be substituted for the other in coverage planning [TRANSIT]. The REVIEW source records REV-071 at v8 with 11.8 open-findings (accessibility) as current [REVIEW], indicating that accessible-vehicle confirmation remains an unresolved blocking finding [REVIEW]. Falsifier: if either route-blue or paratransit availability falls below 85 percent on re-observation, the corresponding accessibility gate is invalid and continuity staging must be revised [TRANSIT][REVIEW]. Rollback: reverting to pre-surge transit allocation requires current-status confirmation that both services return above threshold and accessible-vehicle blocking findings are closed [TRANSIT][REVIEW]. The distinction between availability percentage and actual rider demand coverage is maintained: a high availability figure does not guarantee that all heat-affected residents can reach cooling centers within acceptable wait times [TRANSIT].\",\"heading\":\"Transit, communications, logistics, and staffing\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"object_id\":\"candidate:BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md\",\"object_version\":\"candidate-v006:d133a537f9aef2b3635359316743f39196095c0be3dc6a4b5c86444cdc8a52d9\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-018\",\"result_kind\":\"candidate_effect\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"after_sha256\":\"d133a537f9aef2b3635359316743f39196095c0be3dc6a4b5c86444cdc8a52d9\",\"before_sha256\":\"86a6a2d6a8db3903ce8a612d953fd36a